Table full name: FDA.FDIC_BANKS.INSTITUTIONS
Column name: state_name Type: TEXT Description: State in which the the institution is physically located. The FDIC Act defines state as any State of the United States, the District of Columbia, and any territory of the United States, Puerto Rico, Guam, American Samoa, the Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands, the Virgin Island, and the Northern Mariana Islands.
Column name: zip_code Type: TEXT Description: The first three, four, or five digits of the full postal zip code representing physical location of the institution or its branch office.
Column name: state Type: TEXT Description: 2 letter postal abbreviation for the state in which the the headquarters are physically located. The FDIC Act defines state as any State of the United States, the District of Columbia, and any territory of the United States, Puerto Rico, Guam, American Samoa, the Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands, the Virgin Island, and the Northern Mariana Islands.
